id: pm-5sm91o
title: "GH-714: linked-test verbose child stdout still aborts with EAGAIN after bounded-drain fix"
description: "The published bounded linked-test output drain still allows a verbose Bun child to abort while the identical quality command passes directly. Reproduce below the disclosed capture cap, distinguish transport backpressure from assertion failure, keep pipes draining through child completion, and preserve bounded disclosed output."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T01:00:16.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T12:44:30.704Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T12:43:44.062Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic verbose-child regression reproduces the released EAGAIN path without excessive fixture output; Linked tests continuously drain child pipes through completion while bounding retained and disclosed output; Transport truncation and failures are classified separately from product assertion failures; Node and Bun subprocess acceptance plus full repository gates pass
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: Linked-test child output is captured through blocking regular files with bounded retained output and explicit truncation disclosure.
expected_result: Verbose Node and Bun children complete without EAGAIN while disclosed output stays bounded and transport truncation is not a test failure.
actual_result: Focused suite passes and a packed Bun child emitted 22 MB successfully with truncation notice and zero max-buffer failures.
